# UX-SPEC.md §5.1 · §Board ("The pane") · ADR 0023 — every board key has a control, and the
# board is worked by pointer end to end: a column's `+` opens New card with that column chosen,
# a click selects a card, its ⋯ holds every picker, and the header's `New card` is the `c` key.
#
# The `+` is the one control here that no key reproduces exactly: `c` files a card in the board's
# default column, and `+` files it in the column it sits on. The oracle is the column's badge and
# `board.cards`, which the card lands in with the cursor on it.
#
# Virtual-lane only: it clicks and takes shots.
fixture: board
await idle 20000
key g b
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert lists.board.rows[1].label == "Todo" && lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "2"
assert targets["board.new"] exists && targets["board.filter"] exists
assert targets["board.column[1].add"] exists
shot board

# Todo's `+` opens New card on Todo, with the title already taking the keyboard.
click board.column[1].add
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await idle 10000
assert dialog.name == CardCreate && dialog.fields[0].focused == true
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Todo"
type Seed the board preset
key enter
await overlay absent 10000
await lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "3" 10000
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Todo"
await lists["board.cards"].selected.label == "Seed the board preset" 10000

# A click selects a card, and the selected card shows its ⋯, which holds the pickers.
click board.column[0].card[1]
await focused == "board.column[0].card[1]" 5000
await targets["board.column[0].card[1].menu"] exists 5000
click board.column[0].card[1].menu
await targets["menu.item[0]"] exists 5000
shot card-menu
click menu.item[0]
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert dialog.name == CardPicker
key escape
await overlay absent 10000

# The header's primary button is `c`: New card in the board's default column.
click board.new
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert dialog.name == CardCreate
key escape
await overlay absent 10000
dump pointer
quit
